auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{apiKey}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

docs {
  # selfmemory

  Knowledge-page memory endpoints.

  ## Setup

  1. Run the server: `make run` (listens on :8081)
  2. Create a project API key: `POST /api/projects/{id}/api-keys`
  3. Put it in the `local` environment as `apiKey`

  A project API key is pinned to one project, so `project_id` in a request
  body is optional — send it only to assert which project you expect, and
  the server rejects a mismatch rather than silently using the key's own.

  ## Two read paths

  `Ask` is one model call over full-text hits — fast, single-hop.
  `Research` runs an agent over a materialized copy of the pages. Slower by
  an order of magnitude, and the only path that follows `[[links]]` between
  pages. It needs the `opencode` binary on the server's PATH; without it the
  endpoint returns 503 and `Ask` still works.
}
